    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The change is implemented and the test suite is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, `BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## What I did\n\nThe app stores the **business-day-adjusted registration date** (the controller already rolls weekends/holidays forward before persisting), so all fiscal-year values derive from `Owner.registrationDate`.\n\n**`Owner.java`** (`model/Owner.java`):\n- Added `fiscalYearOf(LocalDate)` \u2014 a fiscal year starts **1 July** and is labelled by the calendar year it ends in (Australian convention, matching the app's NSW/VIC/QLD locale): July\u2013December \u2192 next year, January\u2013June \u2192 that year.\n- Added `getFiscalYear()` returning `FY<YY>` (last two digits of the fiscal year), `null` until the registration date is set.\n- **Membership identifier**: `getMembershipNumber()` now uses the fiscal year's last two digits for its `-M<YY>` segment instead of the raw registration-date year.\n- **Tenure**: `getMembershipPoints()` now awards the 3 tenure points when `fiscalYearOf(today) - fiscalYearOf(registrationDate) > 0` (at least one elapsed fiscal year) rather than a 365-day window. A newly created owner still has zero tenure, so it never earns these points.\n- Removed the now-unused `ChronoUnit` import.\n\n**`openapi.yml`**: added the `fiscalYear` readOnly property to the `Owner` schema (so the generated DTO carries it and MapStruct maps `getFiscalYear()` automatically), and updated the `membershipNumber` and `membershipPoints` descriptions to the fiscal-year wording.\n\nThe audit output confirms consistency: an owner registered `2026-10-02` (October \u2192 FY27) gets `membershipNumber=NSW-16E6609E-M27` and `fiscalYear` `FY27`.\n\nOne behavioural note worth flagging: this intentionally changes existing behaviour (membership numbers for July\u2013December registrations now use the *next* year's `YY`), exactly as the spec requires.",
