    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is clean, additive, and idiomatic for this file:\n\n- **`fiscalYearOf(LocalDate)` is at the right level.** A single private static helper centralizes the \"fiscal year starts 1 July\" rule, and all three consumers (`getFiscalYear`, `getMembershipNumber`, `getMembershipPoints`) reuse it. No duplication of the month-boundary logic. This matches the file's existing convention of keeping date-derived logic inline (e.g. `getAgeBand` uses `Period` directly) rather than reaching for a separate util class.\n\n- **`getFiscalYear()` fits the established shape** of the surrounding `@Transient` derived getters: null-guard, `String.format`, thorough Javadoc, placed logically right after its helper and beside the membership getters it relates to.\n\n- **The \"business-day-adjusted registration date\" wording is coherent, not a missing reuse.** The business-day roll (`toBusinessDay`) is applied in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` before the owner is persisted, so `this.registrationDate` already holds the adjusted date by the time these getters read it. Reading `this.registrationDate` directly is correct placement \u2014 the model shouldn't re-import the controller's holiday table.\n\n- **Good hygiene:** the now-unused `ChronoUnit` import is removed, and the `openapi.yml` schema gains `fiscalYear` with descriptions kept in sync with the Javadoc.\n\n- The slight repetition of `... % 100` two-digit truncation between `getFiscalYear` and `getMembershipNumber` is not worth extracting \u2014 the shared abstraction is `fiscalYearOf`, and having `getMembershipNumber` independently format avoids coupling it to the `FY`-prefixed string. Leaving them independent is the cleaner choice.\n\nA maintainer of this codebase would find this natural.",
